{.i zoi gy. gift gy. xe fanva ma la lojban}
means
' "gift" is the translation of what to Lojban?'
whereas you need
{.i ma xe fanva zoi gy. gift gy. la lojban} = 'What is the translation of
"gift" to Lojban?'



2014-05-17 17:29 GMT+04:00 <aquarius7373@gmail.com>:

> I'm not sure if I got that question right, I just watched the YT video on
> it.
>
> I'm trying to translate Joanna into lojban.
> Joanna means 'God's gift', and God is cevni cev cei. What's gift?
>
> Also, as an example, if I use dunda as gift, would the name be ceidu'a?
> Wouldn't that be God giver?
>
> On another note, my name is Nick, and Nicholas means The people's victory.
> person = prenu pre
> win = jinga jig ji'a
> So could Nicholas be preji'a?
>
> Thanks in advance!
>
> (possibly)-preji'a
